     During[0m[2m step[0m[2m 2,[0m[2m other checkout[0m[2m tasks can[0m[2m run[0m[2m,[0m[2m check stock[0m[2m, and[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m. So[0m[2m by[0m[2m the time[0m[2m we[0m[2m reach[0m[2m step[0m[2m 3,[0m[2m stock might[0m[2m already[0m[2m be[0m[2m 0.[0m[2m
     
     So the[0m[2m issue is[0m[2m NOT in[0m[2m `inventory[0m[2m.decrement[0m[2m()`[0m[2m alone[0m[2m ([0m[2mit's fine[0m[2m in asyncio[0m[2m), but[0m[2m in[0m[2m `[0m[2mcheckout.py[0m[2m` which[0m[2m does[0m[2m check[0m[2m,[0m[2m then charge[0m[2m ([0m[2mlong[0m[2m await[0m[2m), then[0m[2m decrement.[0m[2m
     
     This[0m[2m confirms[0m[2m that[0m[2m fixing[0m[2m `checkout[0m[2m.py`[0m[2m to[0m[2m just[0m[2m call `[0m[2mdecrement[0m[2m`[0m[2m first[0m[2m (and[0m[2m use[0m[2m its return[0m[2m value)[0m[2m will[0m[2m fix the[0m[2m overselling[0m[2m issue.[0m[2m And adding[0m[2m a[0m[2m lock to[0m[2m `Inventory[0m[2m` for[0m[2m all[0m[2m methods[0m[2m is good[0m[2m defensive programming[0m[2m but[0m[2m not strictly[0m[2m necessary if[0m[2m we fix[0m[2m `checkout[0m[2m.py`.[0m[2m
     
     However[0m[2m, looking[0m[2m at `[0m[2minventory[0m[2m.py`[0m[2m more[0m[2m carefully,[0m[2m `increment[0m[2m` also[0m[2m does[0m[2m:[0m[2m
